Falsifies `system_tests::user::running_space_tests::a_corpse_does_not_keep_a_space_rooted_in_a_destroyed_region`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the region sweep leaves a corpse's space alone, which is the shape the tree had before
§249 (a running address space stays nameable) put bound spaces in the registry. The region comes
back while the corpse still owns a root in it, and the revocation registry goes on naming that
root and the log pages the region just handed back.

Expected to fail: the assertion after the region's `DESTROY`, that the corpse's space is gone.

diff --git a/kernel/src/user/address_space_registry.rs b/kernel/src/user/address_space_registry.rs
--- a/kernel/src/user/address_space_registry.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/user/address_space_registry.rs
@@ -459,7 +459,7 @@ pub fn reap_address_spaces_in_region(base: u64, end: u64) {
                         None => in_span,
                         Some(holder) => match binder(holder) {
                             crate::sched::Binder::Gone => true,
-                            crate::sched::Binder::Corpse => in_span,
+                            crate::sched::Binder::Corpse => false,
                             crate::sched::Binder::CanRun => false,
                         },
                     };
